**Problem.** The client sends `IDLE` after five minutes without mouse or keyboard input (rsprot's
`Idle` doc: 15,000 client cycles). On OSRS that logs the player out. OpenRune has no listener for
it, so idle players stay logged in.

**Change.**
- `IdleHandler` sets `manualLogout`, the same flag as the logout button, so `PlayerLogoutProcess`
  applies the same checks (combat etc.). Ignored while a logout is already pending.
- Server-wide toggle `gameplay.idle-logout` in `game.yml` (`GameplayConfig.idleLogout`, next to
  `level-up-popups`), default `true` as on live. With `false` the handler ignores `IDLE` and idle
  players stay logged in. Documented in `game.example.yml`; an existing `game.yml` without the key
  gets the default.

**Tests.** None (removed `IdleHandlerTest` as asked in review). Checked in game (desktop RuneLite, fresh account): with the default `idle-logout: true`, the client was logged out after about 5-6 idle minutes; with `idle-logout: false` (boot log shows `idleLogout=false`), it was still logged in after 8 idle minutes. IDLE while logout is blocked by combat was not tried.

Gate run on upstream `main` bcdb03292 + this branch (a clean merge; `main` touches none of this branch's files up to 731fd392a). Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container, no build or configuration cache, one run per step: `freshCache` + `mergePluginGamevals` pass, `buildCache` pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble` pass, `test` pass (708 tests, 0 failures), `integration` pass (79 tests, 0 failures), boot to "Server ready" pass.

**Caveats.** If logout is blocked (in combat), the player gets the logout button's message, and the
client won't send IDLE again until the next five idle minutes. We have not checked what live does
in that case.

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): Idle, "Logout timer" (players idle for 5 minutes are logged out, if out of combat). rsprot's `Idle` message documentation (sent after 15,000 client cycles without input).

**Release note.** Players are logged out after five idle minutes, as on OSRS; servers can turn this
off with `gameplay.idle-logout: false`.

